WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.991
Cardiac arrest in weightlessness.

2
00:00:03.031 --> 00:00:07.689
Every second counts. Here's how to keep
the blood moving when nothing stays put.

3
00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:12.214
On Earth, your body weight helps you push
down on the chest.

4
00:00:12.254 --> 00:00:14.782
In orbit, every push sends you floating
away,

5
00:00:14.782 --> 00:00:17.141
and your compressions lose their strength.

6
00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:19.562
So you brace yourself.

7
00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.915
Wrap your legs around the patient's chest,

8
00:00:21.915 --> 00:00:25.108
or plant your feet on the ceiling and push
with your arms.

9
00:00:26.008 --> 00:00:29.466
As soon as you can, strap the patient to
the medical table.

10
00:00:30.366 --> 00:00:34.798
Push hard and fast: one hundred to one
hundred and twenty times a minute.

11
00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:38.682
Meanwhile, a crewmate brings the
defibrillator,

12
00:00:38.682 --> 00:00:42.175
sticks on the pads, and follows its voice
instructions.

13
00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:47.863
Swap rescuers every two minutes:
compressions in orbit are exhausting.

14
00:00:48.763 --> 00:00:51.407
Practice in the cardiac arrest simulation,

15
00:00:51.407 --> 00:00:54.491
with your whole crew, until it becomes
automatic.

